WEBVTT

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:04.980
Can I finish now?

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.360
Not yet.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:08.480
It's too early.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:11.860
But...

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.640
Stay calm.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.240
Don't be so aggressive.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.090
That's it.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:19.450
Keep going deeper.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.040
It's sucking me in.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.670
Stay calm. Hold on just a little longer.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.060
I'm home.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.070
Kyo-san. Saku-chan.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.010
Welcome home.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:19.950
Welcome home.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.260
Did you catch any oval squid, Kyo-nii?

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:27.160
Yup. I finally caught one, thankfully.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.740
You actually caught one?

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.610
I guess trying every day, since the 
start of summer break, really paid off.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:39.340
I would have preferred if you'd never caught 
anything and just got sick of fishing.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:46.060
Oval squid sashimi is 
good, though. I like it.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.420
We have mail.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.060
It looks like it's for you guys.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.060
<b>To Lien de Famille</b>

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.070
Welcome to Soryu Island

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:02.570
They want the kids' band to play at an 
island community revitalization event, huh?

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.080
It sounds sketchy.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:13.180
"We will pay for all expenses, including 
for guardians. Please consider our offer.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:17.090
Soryu Island Tourism 
Association Special Advisory

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.300
Aigae Yuzuha."

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.590
It sounds too good to be true.

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.140
Doesn't it?

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.900
I suppose we're getting some attention,

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.050
now that we have that 
promotional video online.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:34.580
I don't know about us getting 
a gig so quickly, though.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.110
It might be a scam or something.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.860
We've been tricked?

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.780
We can't go to the southern islands?

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.240
I wanted to nap on the beach.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:51.380
It sucks, but I don't think we should reply.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.300
Wait.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:58.560
Aside from a bit of beach, 
nearly the whole island is rocky cliffs.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.380
What?

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.260
A sandy, rocky island.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.310
It must be really remote.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:09.010
They probably don't get many tourists. 
It's untouched and pristine.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.510
I bet this island...

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:14.020
is a great fishing spot!

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.660
I think that about does it.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:38.290
I'll have them listen to it tomorrow 
so we can fill in the details.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.840
Kiriyume

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.840
Hibiki~ How've you been?
Can we chat when you have some time?

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:48.950
<i>She sounds way too friendly for Kiriyume.</i>

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.340
I apologize for my absence.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.690
I truly regret making you wait.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.270
What's going on?

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.360
Why are you so formal?

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:01.820
You aren't angry?

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.750
Of course I'm not angry.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:09.410
That's why I tried to talk gently, 
so you wouldn't think I am.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.580
You're so dense.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:12.220
Oh, I see.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:13.330
Sorry.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:16.900
I've been so busy with the band, 
I haven't been spending time with you.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.580
So I was sure you were angry.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.150
O-Of course not.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.670
That aside, though...

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:29.300
Well? The band girls were 
super happy, weren't they?

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.910
You must have gotten the letter about now.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.080
The invitation to island revitalization.

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:37.640
You were the one who sent that letter?

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:41.330
I got asked to help out by a tourism agency,

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:44.440
so I figured I'd pitch you guys like crazy.

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:47.890
You get internet on that island, huh?

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.230
Hey!

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.700
Sorry, I shouldn't have said that.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.270
Jeez.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.700
Do you think it's some 
kind of deserted island?

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.960
Are you sure about this, though?

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:02.060
Don't you want to hire some professionals 
with better name recognition,

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.020
if you're trying to bring 
people to the island?

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.700
You don't need to worry.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.890
This is the first time we're 
doing an island revitalization.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:10.720
We don't really know what 
we're doing, either.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.130
So we'd rather just invite 
people who are eager to come,

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:19.110
so that there's no pressure on us.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:22.930
Besides, I'd like to meet 
the band members, too.

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.170
Jun and the girls?

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.050
Yeah.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:29.630
I watched the promotional video a few 
times, and they started growing on me.

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:32.070
I'm a total fan now.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:33.830
Kiriyume...

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:35.410
All right.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.450
In that case...

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.410
Will you do it?

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:41.190
Everyone seemed interested.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.610
I'm sure I can bring you good news.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:44.730
Really?

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:47.920
In that case, I'll email 
you more event details.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.260
Thanks.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:53.930
By the way, there's something 
I want to give you, too.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.190
Is it a new song?

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:07.240
Yeah.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.270
I finished it just now.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:11.200
It's just a sample export 
with digital vocals, but...

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.710
What do you think?

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:34.430
It has a different vibe than usual.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:36.760
But it's not bad.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.060
Really?

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:39.460
Yeah.

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:42.770
It might be my favorite one so far.

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:44.380
Thank goodness.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:48.630
I'm not used to this style, so I 
couldn't tell if it was good or not.

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:52.530
So, why is it you're having
me listen to your new song?

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:58.570
I'd appreciate if you could make a drawing 
based on the song, like you used to.

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:00.910
Like I used to, huh?

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:04.210
I thought you no longer needed my help.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.050
Of course not.

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:08.800
I really like your art.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.840
If it's okay with you, I want us to 
continue working together going forward.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.500
O-Oh, really?

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:20.100
If you're <i>that</i> charmed 
by me, I will consider it.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.600
Please.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:29.730
So Kiriyume-san wrote that letter?

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:31.040
Yeah.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:33.550
I was shocked when she 
told me yesterday, too.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:37.240
Wasn't Kiriyume the one who did 
illustrations for your music?

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:38.410
Huh...

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.240
You sure know a lot about Kyo.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.830
Wh-What are you...

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.950
I like Kiriyume's art, too.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:49.960
I like her, too, ever since Saku-chan 
told me she's really good.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:54.880
In any case, now that we know it was Kyo's 
acquaintance who sent us the invitation,

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.970
we don't have to worry about it being a scam.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.350
Yes.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.640
So it's up to you guys.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.540
Of course.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.480
I still want to put on a concert there.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:08.610
I'd love to meet Kiriyume-san.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:11.700
I'm going to nap on a southern island,

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:15.570
play at a concert, and become
friends with Kiriyume.

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:17.570
All right, it's settled.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:20.830
Yeah!

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:25.580
So why are you the most 
enthusiastic about this, Sakura?

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.580
Hibiki walked straight into it.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:37.490
The whole thing is a trap to lure in 
those little Lien de Famille brats,

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:41.290
get them on my side, and take them down.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:46.810
I'm going to make them pay dearly 
for coming between Hibiki and me.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.140
That's right.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:51.060
Hibiki needs only to look at me.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:54.460
I'll get rid of anyone who gets in 
my way, by any means necessary.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:57.440
To that end,

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:02.280
I'll make myself the 
ruthless god of Soryu Island.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:10.040
All right, we're all packed.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:12.920
Rock, paper, scissors.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.810
Uh...

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:20.950
What is this?

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:23.560
The result of a fair fight.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.700
Okay, here we go.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:30.020
Lien de Famille's first tour.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.070
Yeah!

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:46.540
Kyo-san, look, you can see it.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.420
So that's Soryu Island.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:56.170
It's a lot smaller than the other 
islands that the ferry passed by.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.670
It's a cute island.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:02.470
The perfect size for a nap.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:22.220
Members of
<b>Lien de Famille</b>

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.850
Welcome to Soryu Island.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:26.330
My name is Ogi Sayuri. 
I'm with the tourism agency.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:29.220
I'm Sawatari Masayoshi, their guardian.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.990
Toriumi Sakura, an attendant.

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:34.960
Thank you for your invitation.

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:39.150
I'm in charge of the coming event.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:41.600
Please let me know if you need anything.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.590
You must be Lien de Famille.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:49.110
I'm Goto Jun, the vocalist and guitarist.

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:53.370
I-I-I look forward to 
doing business with you.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:56.700
I'm Momijidani Nozomi, vocalist and bassist.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:59.590
Kaneshiro Sora.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:00.860
Drums.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.380
Nice to meet you.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:03.710
I'm Nukui Kyo.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:07.490
We finally get to meet, Hibiki-san.

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:10.700
So that means you're Kiriyume?

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:11.740
Yes.

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:15.170
It's a little embarrassing 
being called that in person.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:18.820
My real name is Aigae Yuzuha.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:22.970
I volunteer at the island's 
tourism association.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.690
I see.

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:27.470
I'm surprised, you seem so 
different than you do in chat.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:28.910
I'm sorry.

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:35.230
I'm actually younger than you are, 
and yet I boss you around so much online.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.350
Don't worry about it.

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:41.720
In fact, I think I'd prefer if you'd 
talk to me like you usually do,

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:42.850
if that's okay with you.

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:46.990
I mean, we've finally met in person.

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:52.830
Thank you, Hibiki — I mean, Nukui-kun.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.250
If you'll allow me, I'll talk 
to you as I always have.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:56.630
Okay.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:04.580
Hey, are you okay with that?

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:06.110
With what?

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:16.590
We're staying here?

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:19.100
It's gorgeous.

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.530
Ideal for a nap.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.940
I'm glad you seem to like our resort.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:25.530
Yes.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:26.930
Welcome.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.590
We've been waiting for you.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:29.870
This is my husband.

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:32.990
Ask him if you ever need anything.

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:35.500
<b>Great Amberjack
Length: 150cm
Weight: 50kg</b>

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:35.500
<b>Ojiro Kenta</b>

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:37.620
Wow...

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:40.500
It's big, isn't it?

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:44.050
We don't get many <i>this</i> big,

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:47.660
but you can catch great amberjacks around 
20 kilograms even from the levee.

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:50.300
And if you're lucky, you can 
even catch yellowtail amberjack.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:52.430
<i>20 kilograms!</i>

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:54.430
<i>Yellowtail amberjack!</i>

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.180
Honey!

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.560
Sorry, I get carried away.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.020
I'll show you around the island.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.250
If you're going to show us around...

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:06.230
Take us to this levee.

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:07.650
Please!

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:11.240
Okay, I'm going to go give them a tour.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.160
Watch us come back with a huge catch.

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:15.630
See you!

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:21.890
Sorry. My husband is a hopeless fishing nut.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:25.670
Nah, I don't think we're any better.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:29.930
Why don't we go hang out, too, then?

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:34.430
I wouldn't have thought 
you'd find a place like this

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:36.650
within walking distance from the resort.

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:38.010
Nukui-kun.

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:51.990
Kyo-nii.

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:56.610
I can't tie it.

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:58.200
Help me.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:03.500
Don't go out naked, Ku-chan!

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:07.130
I'm not naked, though, I'm wearing a bottom.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:25.480
I got it on properly.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.190
You all look cute.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.750
O-Of course we do.

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:30.850
You have good taste.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.750
Saku-chan picked these out for us.

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:36.590
What do you think?

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:37.490
It's cute, right?

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.730
Floaty, floaty...

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:48.670
Here I go, Jun.

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:49.770
Take that!

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:53.070
I'm not stopping.

00:15:56.710 --> 00:15:59.380
Nukui-kun, there's a 
hermit crab at your feet!

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:00.850
Sora's drifting away!

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:02.220
No, Sora!

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:05.310
Stay in the cove, or you'll get washed out to sea!

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:08.950
My swimsuit string!

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.660
Don't look this way, Nukui-kun!

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:12.730
Kyo-san!

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:15.740
My swimsuit top got washed away!

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:20.660
I don't know about clinging 
to my back to hide, though.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:25.850
Nukui-kun, would you mind 
rubbing suntan lotion on me?

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:28.800
Hey, Kyo, I'm getting cold.

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.180
Can you rub my belly?

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:31.170
That's not good.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:33.710
All right, I can handle this.

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:34.620
Are you okay?

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:35.430
Yeah.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.470
What is his deal?

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:38.930
Is he actually a pedophile?

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:43.950
I was trying to be sexy to 
tear him away from the brats.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:45.420
Whatever.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.500
I have plenty of time.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.780
It's just the start.

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:50.190
Just the start.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:58.870
Soryu Island Central Community Center

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:13.290
Good work.

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:16.130
The Lien de Famille members are here.

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.010
It's them.

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:24.550
It's the girls Yuzu-chan 
showed us on the computer.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:28.880
They're so adorable, 
and they perform so well.

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:30.020
I'm impressed.

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:34.340
It's going to be so fun performing together.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:37.530
We old folks are going to have to 
put our backs into it for once.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.040
How was the island taiko drumming?

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:49.170
It really hits your belly.

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:50.970
It was so powerful.

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:52.840
I was overwhelmed.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:55.340
We have to keep up.

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.880
We're going to have to do 
extra well at the concert.

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:07.170
Is this the...

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:07.640
Yes.

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:11.360
It's normally a parking lot,

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.650
but this is going to be the 
stage on the day of the concert.

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:20.890
And that over there is the 
entrance to Kiryu Shrine.

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:25.130
Legend has it that there are 
two dragons on this island.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:31.750
Kiryu, a guardian deity, keeps the black 
dragon from bringing calamity to the island.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.690
It's kind of a strange shrine.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.140
You're right.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.560
There's no gate.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:51.400
The wind is strong all year
around on this island,

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.820
but it's especially strong in this area.

00:18:55.340 --> 00:19:01.570
So this shrine's been built to protect 
the <i>mitamashiro</i> even if there's a storm.

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:03.830
Mitamashiro?

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:08.420
It's like a physical proxy 
for worshiping Kiryu-sama.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:13.570
Yuzu-chan, can you take 
care of them for a bit?

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.820
I'm going to perform ministrations.

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:17.840
Okay, got it.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:19.240
Ministrations?

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:20.950
Giving services.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:24.180
Cleaning up the premises, 
trimming the lawn...

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:28.520
The people on the island take 
turns protecting Kiryu Shrine.

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:40.030
Nukui-kun...

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:46.780
There's something I want to show you guys.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.100
Is this what you wanted to show me?

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:18.690
Yes.

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:32.090
It's amazing.

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.290
How was this drawn?

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:38.210
It's Kiriyume's drawing in real life.

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:49.470
I couldn't help but want to show you, 
since you're actually here, Nukui-kun.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.730
You made this for the new song, didn't you?

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:53.980
Yes.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:55.510
It's been a while since I've had a request.

00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:56.890
I was so happy.

00:20:57.300 --> 00:21:01.110
Maybe that's why I ended up drawing it here.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:08.780
Um...

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:12.290
Could you please keep it a 
secret from the islanders?

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:15.870
I might get in trouble if they 
find out I drew this here.

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:17.540
All right.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.020
I won't tell anyone.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:29.010
<b>Surprise Invitation</b>

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:02.740
Damn it, why did I show him?

00:23:02.740 --> 00:23:05.980
I never actually had the 
intention of showing him!

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:08.070
It's fine.

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:09.900
It's a bit of a misstep,

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:11.770
but starting tomorrow,

00:23:11.770 --> 00:23:14.740
I'm going to give the brats a taste 
of hell they'll never forget.

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:20.090
You don't need to enjoy 
your time on this island.

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:22.750
Nobody does.

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:29.350
I'm sorry I messed up trying to be sexy.

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>#08  The Girl in the Mural</b>

00:23:29.350 --> 00:23:32.810
I even ended up showing him 
something I never wanted to.

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:38.550
I wonder if it might have worked if 
I'd shown him something more sexy...

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:38.970
Wholesome anime!
